christine lagarde the european central  bank president has some really choice  words about cryptocurrencies in the last  couple of days on a recent episode of  college tour a european talk show she  started talking about cryptocurrencies  and how she thinks they're worthless but  then she hit us with the dichotomy and  so first if christine lagarde the  european central bank thinks bitcoin is  worthless why exactly is that well  here's what she said the first thing was  she said my very humble assessment is  that it is worth nothing great very  descriptive then she went on to state it  is based on nothing there is no  underlying asset to act as an anchor of  safety and sure maybe that's true or  maybe it's not but if christine legard  and other central bankers in europe  actually believe that bitcoin and  cryptocurrencies are worthless then the  conversation basically would stop there  and the market will ultimately prove  them right and those assets will end up  being worthless right well there's a  catch the ecb and christine lagarde they  also want to regulate bitcoin and  cryptocurrencies she went on to say in  that exact same talk show that i'm  concerned about those people who think  it's going to be a reward who have no  understanding of the risks who will lose  it all and who will be terribly  disappointed which is why i believe that  they should be regulated now of course  in this scenario there's two different  paths that you can pursue the first is  that the central bankers actually do  believe that these assets are going to  end up being worthless and they simply  want regulation in place to try to  prevent people from buying them or the  second is that the central bankers don't  actually believe that these are going to  be worthless assets and instead they  realize they can't shut it down there is  no grounds for them to stop the free  market competition between the central  bank assets and these new digital assets  and instead in that scenario they simply  want to regulate them so that they can  get some level of control  now the central bankers will tell you  they don't actually believe there's any  value here but i think that reality is  closer to they understand that there's  value and they simply want regulation in  place so they can still have some  semblance of control regardless of what  happens saying something's worthless and  then making a case for regulating it  doesn't make a lot of sense we simply  are watching them talk out of two sides  of their mouth central bankers they have  their hands full they're going to have  to deal with the changing macro  landscape they literally are trying to  figure out what their monetary policy is  going to be for the next decade and at  the same time they have that nagging  nagging industry of bitcoin and  cryptocurrencies at their heels it'll be  fascinating to watch how this plays out  but christine lagarde making sure  everyone knows bitcoin and  cryptocurrencies are worthless and she  also wants to regulate them hey you did  you like this video great we make five  of them a day and post them here on this  channel make sure you subscribe like the  video and see you next time
 

